      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Goñi Urriza et al.",
        "AbstractText": "Desulfovibrio BerOc1 is a sulfate-reducing bacterium isolated from the Berre lagoon (French Mediterranean coast). BerOc1 is able to methylate and demethylate mercury. The genome size is 4,081,579 bp assembled into five contigs. We identified the hgcA and hgcB genes involved in mercury methylation, but not those responsible for mercury demethylation."
      },
